{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`review_plan_start(ticket)` returns a `job_id`; callers then poll `gate_status(job_id)` and, when the job is terminal, read the retained `REVIEW_RESULT` findings for remediation. Today `gate_status` can report a plan-review run as terminal (`status: \"passed\"`, `verdict: \"BLOCK\"`) without giving the caller any per-run proof that the `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar for that same run is the sidecar now readable from the tickets tracker. A caller that reads \"latest findings\" in that state can silently consume the previous run's findings.\n\nObserved 2026-09-01 while remediating `responsive-undamaged-auklet` (`549b-9cc5-940e-46c3`): job `1788326596882647223-94573cf0d90d404e87c74855306c16f2` reported terminal BLOCK, but the newest readable `REVIEW_RESULT` was `1788325963941841589-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json` from the prior run. The current run's sidecar appeared later as `1788327281362056852-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json`.\n\n## Root cause / actual layer\n\nThe in-process write order is not simply \"terminal index before `sidecar.emit()`\": `review_plan()` calls `sidecar.emit()` synchronously before `_mcp_llm._spawn_gate_daemon()` records the terminal `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>` entry in `finally`. The defect is the missing per-run sidecar receipt/generation in that terminal entry and status response:\n\n- `sidecar.emit()` is best-effort and returns only `sidecar_emitted: true|false` on the model verdict.\n- Before this fix, `_spawn_gate_daemon()` discarded that sidecar outcome when writing the terminal run index.\n- `gate_runs.gate_run_status()` reported terminal status from the local run index plus attestation currency only. For BLOCK verdicts the plan-review attestation is unsigned by definition, so the existing `durable` block cannot prove findings readability.\n- `sidecar.latest_review_result(ticket)` returns the newest usable sidecar for the ticket, not a sidecar tied to a specific `job_id` or review generation.\n\nTherefore any terminal run index without an exact sidecar receipt leaves the poller unable to distinguish: current sidecar readable, current sidecar not visible yet in this reader's tracker view, legacy/partial terminal index with unknown generation, or permanent best-effort sidecar failure. That ambiguity is the stale-read bug.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nMake the status contract explicit and additive; do not change verdict computation or make sidecar emission mandatory.\n\n1. When an async plan-review daemon finishes, copy the sidecar outcome into the terminal run index:\n   - `sidecar_emitted: false` when `review_plan()` says the best-effort sidecar did not persist.\n   - `sidecar_emitted: true` plus `sidecar_reviewed_at: <ns timestamp>` when `review_plan()` emitted a sidecar and the daemon can read the newest `REVIEW_RESULT` timestamp after `work()` returns.\n2. Extend `gate_status(job_id)` for plan-review jobs with a `findings` block:\n   - `sidecar_type: \"REVIEW_RESULT\"`\n   - `readable: bool`\n   - `reason: \"current-review-result-sidecar\" | \"review-result-sidecar-missing\" | \"sidecar-not-emitted\" | \"review-result-generation-unknown\" | \"run-<status>\"`\n   - `reviewed_at: int|null` (the expected sidecar timestamp for this run)\n   - `latest_reviewed_at: int|null` (the newest sidecar currently readable for this ticket)\n   - `job_started_at: int|null` only for legacy records with no receipt, for diagnostics.\n3. Mark `findings.readable=true` only when the exact `sidecar_reviewed_at` file exists and parses as a supported `plan_review_result_v1/v2` sidecar. Do not infer freshness from \"latest timestamp after job start\"; that could falsely attribute a later unrelated sidecar to a legacy job.\n4. Permanent failure disposition: if `sidecar_emitted` is false, `gate_status` still reports the terminal verdict but returns `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\"`. A poll-then-read caller must stop treating findings as pending and surface the unavailable findings condition instead of looping forever.\n\nThis honors the existing documented contract by making the missing state observable. It is not an API redesign: existing `status`, `verdict`, and `durable` semantics remain unchanged, and callers that ignore `findings` continue to work as before.\n\n## Scope / file impact\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py`: compute and expose the plan-review findings-readability block from the run index and current tracker sidecar state.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`: record the exact per-run `REVIEW_RESULT` receipt from the completed review result in the terminal async gate index.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py` and `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`: return/stamp the written sidecar event timestamp so the daemon records the sidecar this run actually wrote, not a later newest-by-ticket sidecar.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` and `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`: document/model the additive `findings` status field.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`: regression tests for the actual stale-read window and permanent sidecar failure disposition.\n- `AGENTS.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`: document that plan-review pollers wait for `gate_status(job_id).findings.readable` before reading latest findings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Reproduce the actual window with writer already returned: seed an old `REVIEW_RESULT`, record a terminal run index for a newer job with an expected `sidecar_reviewed_at`, do not create that sidecar yet, and assert `gate_status(job_id)` is terminal but `findings.readable=false` with `reason=\"review-result-sidecar-missing\"` and `latest_reviewed_at` pointing at the older sidecar.\n- [ ] After writing the expected current sidecar file, assert the same job reports `findings.readable=true`, `reason=\"current-review-result-sidecar\"`, and the expected `reviewed_at`.\n- [ ] Drive the documented poll-then-read sequence across two runs and assert it never returns the prior run's findings for the newer job; it returns no findings until the current job's exact sidecar is readable.\n- [ ] Assert permanent sidecar failure is distinguishable: a terminal plan-review run with `sidecar_emitted=false` reports `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\"`.\n- [ ] Assert the daemon records the exact sidecar receipt returned by `review_plan()` even when a newer same-ticket sidecar is already readable, so receipt capture cannot misattribute latest-by-ticket to this job.\n- [ ] Assert legacy terminal records without a per-run receipt report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"review-result-generation-unknown\"`, and expose `job_started_at` only as diagnostics.\n- [ ] Validate with `pytest -q tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`, MCP schema coverage for the touched output model, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing when the plan-review verdict is computed or whether a BLOCK run is considered a completed (`passed`) gate run.\n- Making `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars required for the verdict itself; sidecars remain best-effort observability.\n- Changing `plan_review_status` or signed-attestation currency.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788361936815699001,"uuid":"459f9ae2-41e9-4ced-95f5-a26f3dac1120"}